cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below - and cite Boltz-2, DiffDock and PLIP (see references)."
title: "Boltz-2 MolPort Screening"
abstract: >-
  Prospective virtual screening of a commercial compound catalogue against
  human carbonic anhydrase isoforms II, IV and VII with Boltz-2, followed by
  constraint-based re-ranking of the top hits: DiffDock poses, PLIP interaction
  profiles, and re-prediction with and without the resulting pocket constraint.
  Ranks by a two-stage score that discards low-confidence predictions before
  ordering by predicted affinity. Code only - the screening library and its
  results are not part of the repository; a 100-compound public demo set is
  included so both pipelines can be run end to end.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Mitterbuchner"
    given-names: "Niklas"
    email: "26430420+NikMibu@users.noreply.github.com"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/NikMibu/boltz2-molport-screening"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-08"
keywords:
  - boltz-2
  - virtual-screening
  - drug-discovery
  - natural-products
  - carbonic-anhydrase
  - diffdock
  - plip
  - structural-constraints

